Error codes defined by the Core module. Each entry gives the `code` and the `messageId` of the `Error` that reports it. `descriptionResId` is the string resource of a description of the error; most of these errors also carry that text in `Error.detailedMessage`.

The entries from `NOT_READABLE_FILE` to `MAPS_UPDATE_FAILED` (codes 1 to 7) are reported with `ErrorType.CORE_RESOURCES`, the others with `ErrorType.CORE`. `NO_NETWORK_CONNECTION` and `NO_INTERNET_CONNECTION` are not reported by this version of the SDK.

The native layer of the SDK also reports errors with `ErrorType.CORE`. This enumeration does not list them, and their codes include 10 to 19, the codes of the `ErrorType.CORE` entries here. For example, when `Core.init` cannot build the road network from the maps, it reports code 18, the code of `BUSY`, with an empty messageId. So compare the `messageId` as well as the type and the code:

```kotlin
val isBusy = error.type == ErrorType.CORE && error.messageId == CoreErrorCodes.BUSY.messageId
```

The errors that `Core.init` reports to `onCoreInitError` are:

- `BUSY`;
- with `ErrorType.CORE_RESOURCES`, while it deploys what the app bundles in its assets: `EXTERNAL_STORAGE_NOT_ACCESSIBLE`, `NO_RESOURCES_IN_ASSETS`, `MAPS_UPDATE_FAILED`, and the versioning-file errors `NOT_READABLE_FILE`, `NOT_WRITABLE_FILE`, `INCOMPLETE_VERSIONING_FILE` and `VERSIONING_FILE_NOT_FOUND`;
- with `ErrorType.CORE`, these errors of the native layer, which this enumeration does not list:
- code 5: the license could not be activated, for example because the purchase UUID is missing, or because the device is offline and the app has never activated its license;
- codes 7 to 10: the maps could not be loaded from the maps folder; code 10 comes with an empty messageId;
- code 18, with an empty messageId: the road network could not be built from the maps.

Class that specifies the set of parameters used as filters when looking for compatible charging points. These filters include:

- means of accessibility;
- means of authentication;
- means of payment;
- means of booking;
- a set of connector types;
- a set of current types;
- a minimum power (`minPower`) and a list of operators (`addOperator`).

A new filter already contains four accessibility types: `AccessibilityType.PUBLIC`, `AccessibilityType.PUBLIC_WITH_MEMBERSHIP`, `AccessibilityType.PUBLIC_UPON_PRESENTATION` and `AccessibilityType.OTHER`. `addAccessType` adds to them: to keep other types only, remove these four with `removeAccessType`. The other sets and the list of operators start empty, and `minPower` starts at 0.

Create a filter only once the Core is initialised (see `com.benomad.msdk.core.Core.init`): the constructor needs the Core's native library, which `com.benomad.msdk.core.Core.getInstance` loads. Once `dispose` is called, do not call any other method of the filter.

Contains all the information related to an administrative area (boundary).

`getClassId()` returns the nature of the boundary, as a GDF (Geographic Data Files) code:

- `KB_COUNTRY` (1111): countries;
- `KB_ORDRE_1_AREA` (1112): states, regions, etc.;
- `KB_ORDRE_7_AREA` (1118): departments;
- `KB_ORDRE_8_AREA` (1119): cities;
- `KB_ORDRE_9_AREA` (1120): districts.

The codes 1113 to 1117 are not used. `getName()` returns the name of the area and `getKey` its administrative key.

A semantic attribute of a map object or of a `Form`: an object's semantic definition is its set of attributes.

Each attribute has a type, a value and a numerical code, from 0 to `UINT16_MAX`. The code gives the attribute's meaning: two attributes with the same code have the same meaning. For example, the attribute codes of the maps include the `KB_ATT_` constants of `com.benomad.msdk.core.carto.CartoConst`, such as `KB_ATT_NAME` for the official name. Within one class of objects, two attributes with the same code must have the same type.

There are seven types, each with its subclass:

- `KEY`: `KeyAttribute`, an unsigned numerical key, which may be used for a key/label relation;
- `LABEL`: `LabelAttribute`, an unsigned numerical label, which may be used for a key/label relation;
- `SIGNED`: `SignedAttribute`, a 32-bit signed integer;
- `UNSIGNED`: `UnSignedAttribute`, a 32-bit unsigned integer;
- `FLOAT`: `FloatAttribute`, a float;
- `STRING`: `StringAttribute` and `KeyStringAttribute`, a string;
- `META`: `MetaAttribute`, an array of bytes.

The constructors of the subclasses throw the checked `InvalidAttributeException` when the code or the value is out of range.

The class ID already has a style that the new one cannot replace:

- `com.benomad.msdk.mapping.style.MapStyle.createPolylineStyle`: the class already has a line style (a style for lines and polylines);
- `com.benomad.msdk.mapping.style.MapStyle.createPolygonStyle`: the class already has a polygon style;
- `com.benomad.msdk.mapping.style.MapStyle.createPOIStyle`: the class already has a line style. An existing POI style does not cause this error.
